IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `hdb-flat-schemes`

-- HDB flat schemes as published (read 12 October 2026) -- worked cases. Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING of
-- HDB's published policy, not about law. Expected values are written by hand from the pages.
--
-- The scenario dates (2028, 2031 to 2036, 2042) are in the future. Every answer here is on the policy AS PUBLISHED IN
-- OCTOBER 2026; HDB may change any figure before then without legislation.

§ `The requirements' own questions`

-- REQ-0007 (cradle-to-grave-simone e050, February 2028). Both Singapore citizens, aged 28 and 24, combined income $9,600,
-- no property, no subsidy taken, a new 4-room flat. Eligible: 4-room is within "up to a 5-room flat", both at least 21,
-- $9,600 is within the $16,000 ceiling for a new 4-room flat. Answered on the policy as published in October 2026.
#ASSERT `the couple may apply under the Fiance Fiancee Scheme` 2 0 28 24 9600 `4-room` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 EQUALS TRUE
-- ... and they must solemnise the marriage within 3 months from the completion of the flat purchase.
#ASSERT `the months allowed to solemnise the marriage` EQUALS 3

-- REQ-0018 (cradle-to-grave-simone e07c). Keys collected 15 August 2031 to a new Standard 4-room flat: MOP 5 years, so the
-- flat may first be sold on the open market on 15 August 2036 (key collection taken as completion; NOTES.md finding 2).
-- Answered on the policy as published in October 2026.
#ASSERT `the first day the flat may be sold on the open market` 2031 8 15 `Standard` FALSE EQUALS 20360815

-- REQ-0274 (cradle-to-grave-jun-hao j074, February 2042). A single citizen of 35, unmarried, earning $2,800 a month, no
-- property, a first-timer, applying for a new 2-room Flexi flat. Eligible (age 35, ceiling $8,000).
#ASSERT `the single may apply for a new flat` TRUE FALSE 35 2800 `2-room Flexi` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 EQUALS TRUE
-- The EHG (Singles): $2,800 falls in the band $2,751 to $3,000, so $25,000 -- assuming 12 months' continuous work and a
-- 99-year lease. Answered on the table published from 20 August 2024, as read in October 2026.
#ASSERT `the single qualifies for the EHG` TRUE 35 FALSE TRUE 2800 99 TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the EHG (Singles) for the household` TRUE 20420218 FALSE 2800 EQUALS 25000

§ `Fiance/Fiancee Scheme: the income ceiling by flat type`

#ASSERT `the couple may apply under the Fiance Fiancee Scheme` 2 0 28 24 16000 `4-room` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the couple may apply under the Fiance Fiancee Scheme` 2 0 28 24 16001 `4-room` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 EQUALS FALSE
-- A 3-room project launched with the $8,000 ceiling, and one with $16,000.
#ASSERT `the couple may apply under the Fiance Fiancee Scheme` 2 0 28 24 9600 `3-room` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the couple may apply under the Fiance Fiancee Scheme` 2 0 28 24 9600 `3-room` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 EQUALS TRUE
-- Not "up to a 5-room flat".
#ASSERT `the couple may apply under the Fiance Fiancee Scheme` 2 0 28 24 9600 `executive` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 EQUALS FALSE

§ `Fiance/Fiancee Scheme: citizenship, age, property, subsidies`

-- A fiancee of 20 cannot be an applicant (she may be a core occupier; not encoded).
#ASSERT `the couple may apply under the Fiance Fiancee Scheme` 2 0 28 20 9600 `4-room` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 EQUALS FALSE
-- One citizen and one SPR: allowed.
#ASSERT `the couple may apply under the Fiance Fiancee Scheme` 1 1 28 24 9600 `4-room` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 EQUALS TRUE
-- Owning private residential property bars them.
#ASSERT `the couple may apply under the Fiance Fiancee Scheme` 2 0 28 24 9600 `4-room` FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 0 0 EQUALS FALSE
-- Sold private property 29 months before the HFE application: too soon. 30 months: the wait has run.
#ASSERT `the couple may apply under the Fiance Fiancee Scheme` 2 0 28 24 9600 `4-room` FALSE FALSE TRUE 29 0 0 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the couple may apply under the Fiance Fiancee Scheme` 2 0 28 24 9600 `4-room` FALSE FALSE TRUE 30 0 0 EQUALS TRUE
-- Two non-residential properties: over the limit of 1.
#ASSERT `the couple may apply under the Fiance Fiancee Scheme` 2 0 28 24 9600 `4-room` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 2 0 EQUALS FALSE
-- A core member who has taken two subsidies: may not buy from HDB.
#ASSERT `the couple may apply under the Fiance Fiancee Scheme` 2 0 28 24 9600 `4-room` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 2 EQUALS FALSE

§ `Solemnisation: the last day, on the encoder's month convention`

-- Completion 31 October 2031: 31 January 2032 (across the year end).
#ASSERT `the last day to solemnise the marriage` 2031 10 31 EQUALS 20320131
-- Completion 30 November 2031: 2032 is a leap year, so 29 February 2032.
#ASSERT `the last day to solemnise the marriage` 2031 11 30 EQUALS 20320229

§ `Minimum occupation period by classification`

-- The same keys date, 15 August 2031: a Plus flat (10 years), and a Standard flat under Fresh Start (20 years).
#ASSERT `the first day the flat may be sold on the open market` 2031 8 15 `Plus` FALSE EQUALS 20410815
#ASSERT `the first day the flat may be sold on the open market` 2031 8 15 `Standard` TRUE EQUALS 20510815
-- The day before and the day itself, for REQ-0018's flat.
#ASSERT `the MOP has ended` 2031 8 15 `Standard` FALSE 20360814 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the MOP has ended` 2031 8 15 `Standard` FALSE 20360815 EQUALS TRUE
-- Keys on 29 February 2028: 2033 is not a leap year, so 1 March 2033 (encoder's convention). From 29 February 2032
-- under the Fresh Start Housing Scheme: 2052 is a leap year, so 29 February 2052.
#ASSERT `the first day the flat may be sold on the open market` 2028 2 29 `Standard` FALSE EQUALS 20330301
#ASSERT `the first day the flat may be sold on the open market` 2032 2 29 `Standard` TRUE EQUALS 20520229

§ `Single Singapore Citizen Scheme, new flat`

-- 34: too young for a new flat.
#ASSERT `the single may apply for a new flat` TRUE FALSE 34 2800 `2-room Flexi` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 EQUALS FALSE
-- A new 3-room flat: not open to singles.
#ASSERT `the single may apply for a new flat` TRUE FALSE 35 2800 `3-room` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 EQUALS FALSE
-- Over the $8,000 ceiling.
#ASSERT `the single may apply for a new flat` TRUE FALSE 40 8001 `2-room Flexi` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 EQUALS FALSE
-- A second-timer: only first-timers may buy new.
#ASSERT `the single may apply for a new flat` TRUE FALSE 40 2800 `2-room Flexi` FALSE FALSE 0 0 1 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the additional amount payable by singles for a new flat` EQUALS 15000

§ `EHG (Singles): the bands of the published table`

-- HDB's own example: Mr A, $2,000 a month, a 2-room Flexi flat: $40,000.
#ASSERT `the EHG for a single alone` 2000 EQUALS 40000
#ASSERT `the EHG for a single alone` 4500 EQUALS 2500
#ASSERT `the EHG for a single alone` 4501 EQUALS 0
-- HDB's own example: Miss A and Miss B, $4,000 together, a 2-room Flexi flat: $80,000 ($40,000 each).
#ASSERT `the EHG for two or more singles` 4000 EQUALS 80000
-- HDB's own example (resale): Mr C and Mr D, $4,400 together: $70,000.
#ASSERT `the EHG for two or more singles` 4400 EQUALS 70000

§ `EHG (Singles): eligibility and the published date`

-- $4,600 alone is over $4,500; with another single it is within $9,000.
#ASSERT `the single qualifies for the EHG` TRUE 35 FALSE TRUE 4600 99 TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the single qualifies for the EHG` TRUE 35 TRUE TRUE 4600 99 TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Not in continuous work for 12 months (HDB's Mr C, resale): no EHG.
#ASSERT `the single qualifies for the EHG` TRUE 35 FALSE FALSE 2000 99 TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- An HFE application before 20 August 2024: the published table does not say; the encoding gives nil.
#ASSERT `the EHG (Singles) for the household` TRUE 20240819 FALSE 2800 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the EHG (Singles) for the household` TRUE 20240820 TRUE 4000 EQUALS 80000
